# The graded machines and every container run Linux. A CRLF checkout of a
# shell script breaks it there -- `set -euo pipefail` becomes `set -euo
# pipefail\r`, "invalid option name" -- and an entrypoint's `#!/bin/sh\r`
# fails to exec. Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, so without
# these a Windows clone of this repo produces scripts that only run on
# Windows. eol=lf overrides autocrlf.
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.bat  text eol=crlf
# Redundant -- these live in libs/nexus-proto, whose own .gitattributes
# governs its checkout (a superproject's attributes do not reach into a
# submodule). Repeated here so it is visible where it is depended on:
# proto_hash is over raw .proto bytes, so a CRLF checkout of the submodule
# computes a different hash at the same pin and the handshake refuses.
*.proto text eol=lf
